Apple today seeded the first beta of an upcoming iOS 27.2 update to developers for testing purposes, with the update coming just two days after the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> launch. Apple also seeded an iPadOS 27.2 beta.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" /><br/>
Registered developers can download the beta updates by opting in under Settings > General > Software Update and selecting the &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; developer beta.<br/>
<br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI will be available in new languages later this year, and support could be added in iOS 27.2. Apple is adding French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish in October.<br/>
<br/>
Two <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> features <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/11/ios-27-delayed-features/">were removed</a> from the launch version of &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, and those could also be reintroduced as soon as iOS 27.2. Apple delayed suggestions in Messages conversations and the option to automatically fix compromised and weak passwords using AI.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also plans to debut a new Health app experience, and we could see that in the beta as well. <br/>
<br/>
Apple releasing an iOS 27.2 beta ahead of a iOS 27.1 beta is a surprise, especially because the company plans to ship the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-duo-ios-27-1/">iPhone Duo with iOS 27.1</a>. Apple may be holding iOS 27.1 until the Duo comes out, just to keep the features under wraps. iOS 27.1 will add updated app layouts and features built for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>'s two displays. The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; will have a vertical dock, vertical <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, new dual-screen app layouts, side-by-side app multitasking, and exclusive Camera app capabilities.<br/>
<br/>
